These lemmas make `prop` 1-inductive **together**, assuming a reset clock edge occurs before the property is checked. Without that assumption, the registers may begin unconstrained. The subtraction invariant uses the module’s 8-bit arithmetic. ([fpga.mit.edu](https://fpga.mit.edu/6205/_static/F25/documentation/1800-2017.pdf?utm_source=openai))

<json>
{
  "lemmas": [
    {
      "lemma": "property lemma_1; @(posedge clk) disable iff (rst) (d1 == 8'sd1 && d2 == 8'sd1); endproperty",
      "explanation": "Reset sets both decrement amounts to one, and neither changes afterward."
    },
    {
      "lemma": "property lemma_2; @(posedge clk) disable iff (rst) (x1 == 8'sd0 || x1 == 8'sd1); endproperty",
      "explanation": "Reset sets x1 to one. An enabled update changes it to zero; otherwise it holds. This limits the possible offset between x2 and in."
    },
    {
      "lemma": "property lemma_3; @(posedge clk) disable iff (rst) ((x2 - x1) == (in - 8'sd1)); endproperty",
      "explanation": "The relation holds after reset and persists because enabled updates decrement x1 and x2 equally. Thus x2 is in or in minus one; when in is positive, either value is nonnegative."
    }
  ]
}
</json>

The key difficulty is the decrement: without knowing `d2`, a positive `x2` could become negative in one step. The uninitialized `x3` only controls whether the decrement occurs.

<json>
{
  "lemmas": [
    {
      "lemma": "property lemma_1; @(posedge clk) disable iff (rst) (d2 == 8'sd1); endproperty",
      "explanation": "Reset sets d2 to 1, and no other branch changes it. Thus x2 either holds or, only when positive, decreases by exactly 1. Together with the target property, this makes nonnegativity of x2 when in > 0 inductive."
    }
  ]
}
</json>

This proof requires a clock edge with `rst` asserted before checking begins. `disable iff (rst)` disables checking during reset; it does not itself initialize `d2`. ([accellera.org](https://accellera.org/images/resources/videos/SystemVerilog_Assertions_Tutorial_2016.pdf?utm_source=openai))
